From ebd59be23d12d5afc4cfbac682e37ae515e93d4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:42:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] feat(update): `hermes update --up-to <sha>` stops
 main at a first-parent commit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

hermes-sync (t_01a1d0a6b9097a68) loses whole apply windows on the MacBook when the
ready Desktop prebuild serves an older origin/main commit C (installed < C < tip):
`hermes update` could only move to the tip. With `--up-to C` core fast-forwards
branch main to C instead.

- After the normal fetch, before any tree write or commit point, it requires the
  checkout on branch main, C a commit, HEAD a proper ancestor of C, and C on
  `git rev-list --first-parent HEAD..origin/main`. Any failure prints
  `✗ --up-to <sha10>: <reason>. No update was applied.`, records `up_to_refused`
  and exits 1. It also refuses with --branch/--channel/--set-channel/--check/--plan
  (and --install-id/--list-venv-holders), a malformed sha, and ZIP, image or
  package-managed installs, or a channel that is not branch main.
- The move is `merge --ff-only C` on main (never detach, never the diverged reset).
  The preflight, arm_commit_point, the interrupted-pull marker, _refuse_unselected_head,
  the receipt expected_sha and the fleet restart marker all name C.
- The fork's upstream sync and push are skipped for the run.
- Prints `→ Updating up to <sha10> (origin/main is <tip10>; N commit(s))`.
- `"--up-to"` is in hermes_cli/subcommands/update.py: hermes-sync's capability marker.

main.py stays at its line cap: the --list-venv-holders printing moves into
update_cmd_windows.print_venv_holders (unchanged behaviour).

Proof:
- RED: tests/hermes_cli/test_update_up_to.py on the old tree (module shimmed):
  25/25 failed. GREEN: 27 passed.
- 176 update/old-updater/channel/streaming/subprocess test files: 3327 passed, 0 failed.
- Mutants (sdlc-review mutants.py), 21/21 killed: first-parent check dropped, plain
  rev-list without --first-parent, HEAD-ancestor check dropped, sha==HEAD, branch
  main, commit resolves, tip/HEAD unresolved, sha regex, incompatible flags,
  zip/release/branch install, sync_upstream gate, release_tag gate, zero-count fork
  sync gate, detach gate, diverged-reset gate, target_ref retarget, expected_sha pin,
  gateway resume on both refusal paths, managed and admission refusals.
- scripts/check --only health --base origin/main: ok.
